WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.555
Users and groups are routing tools in
SignalR.

2
00:00:04.635 --> 00:00:11.600
They help the server decide which active
connections should receive a message.

3
00:00:11.680 --> 00:00:16.878
A single user may have several connections
at the same time,

4
00:00:16.958 --> 00:00:22.260
such as a browser tab, a mobile session,
and a desktop client.

5
00:00:22.340 --> 00:00:29.721
The design should account for that
one-to-many relationship when sending targeted

6
00:00:29.801 --> 00:00:32.608
messages or tracking presence.

7
00:00:32.688 --> 00:00:38.614
Group membership should come from trusted
server-side decisions.

8
00:00:38.694 --> 00:00:44.620
A group can represent a room, tenant,
project, role-like audience,

9
00:00:44.700 --> 00:00:50.002
subscription, administrative channel, or
workflow state,

10
00:00:50.082 --> 00:00:55.488
but joining that group should follow the
application policy.

11
00:00:55.568 --> 00:01:01.494
The server should decide whether a
connection belongs in the group,

12
00:01:01.574 --> 00:01:08.331
and it should revisit that decision when
the underlying permission changes.

13
00:01:08.411 --> 00:01:15.689
Groups should not replace identity,
authorization policies, or resource checks.

14
00:01:15.769 --> 00:01:18.783
They can make delivery efficient,

15
00:01:18.863 --> 00:01:25.517
but they do not prove that a caller may
act on a resource or receive a sensitive

16
00:01:25.597 --> 00:01:26.429
message.

17
00:01:26.509 --> 00:01:33.578
A secure design combines authenticated
identity, server-side authorization,

18
00:01:33.658 --> 00:01:36.361
and careful group management.

19
00:01:36.441 --> 00:01:39.560
Presence features need restraint.

20
00:01:39.640 --> 00:01:44.526
Showing that a user is online, typing,
viewing a record,

21
00:01:44.606 --> 00:01:48.661
or active in a room can improve
collaboration,

22
00:01:48.741 --> 00:01:52.483
but it can also reveal sensitive behavior.

23
00:01:52.563 --> 00:01:58.593
Presence should respect tenant boundaries,
privacy expectations,

24
00:01:58.673 --> 00:02:06.054
and the difference between internal
operational signals and user-visible status.

25
00:02:06.134 --> 00:02:12.580
Disconnect and reconnect behavior affects
group membership, presence,

26
00:02:12.660 --> 00:02:15.155
and delivery expectations.

27
00:02:15.235 --> 00:02:21.473
Teams should define what happens when a
connection drops, reconnects,

28
00:02:21.553 --> 00:02:25.087
changes identity, or loses permission.

29
00:02:25.167 --> 00:02:32.341
Real-time delivery is most reliable when
those lifecycle decisions are explicit

30
00:02:32.421 --> 00:02:34.500
instead of accidental.
